38,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
39,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
40,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Oh no! The bin house sounds like a stinky trap! If you can't hose it out, the smell just gets worse in the summer. I don't want our corner to smell like that!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Midori,,"That sounds unpleasant, Rin. I've found that we're spending quite a bit on maintenance—about thirty-four thousand yen a year—just because bags are left open. It seems like a waste of our shared resources.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The complaint log is a masterpiece of obsession. Fourteen entries in three years, and eleven are from a single household. It seems we have a very dedicated critic living right next to the bins.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,May,,And the drama continues! The meeting minutes are just as spicy as I hoped. The station block spent two years fighting over a broken latch and who has to sweep. It's practically a soap opera!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The physical reality is quite restrictive. One frontage is barely ninety centimeters wide, and another is mostly a driveway. Furthermore, the truck arrives as early as 7:40, which complicates any plan involving active management.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, 7:40 is so early! I'd still be dreaming about adventures. If we have to be there that early, it'll be a total drag for everyone, especially if it smells!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Asuka, that is very early. If we want to avoid the maintenance costs I found, we might need a better shelter, but I worry about how we'll afford it given the different budgets we all have.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, if we're worried about budgets, we should probably avoid anything that requires a massive upfront cost. Besides, looking at the complaint log, a fancy shelter won't stop our resident critic from finding something to moan about.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, you're so cynical! But honestly, the residents' meeting statements were the real eye-opener. Nobody wants to be the ""bad guy"" who tells a neighbor their bag is late. We're all just pretending to be polite while avoiding the work!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@May, that avoidance is exactly why we need a formal system. If we rely on ""politeness,"" the burden inevitably falls on whoever is the most passive or the one whose gate is currently being used. We need a concrete plan.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Rin,,"But if we make it too formal, it'll be boring! Still, the next lane's supervised mornings only happen twenty times a year per house. That doesn't sound too bad, as long as we don't have to smell a stinky bin house!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, twenty times a year sounds manageable, but I'm still thinking about the money. If we build a new shelter, it could cost over two hundred thousand yen, even with the ward subsidy. That's a lot for some of us.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, spending two hundred thousand yen just to appease a few complaints seems like a poor investment. We should focus on a solution that doesn't bankrupt us or require a four-month bureaucratic nightmare.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,May,,"@Asuka, you hit the nail on the head! It's always the same story—someone ends up doing all the heavy lifting while everyone else just smiles. I'm not interested in becoming the neighborhood's unpaid concierge!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@May, exactly. The current situation is an invisible burden. If we simply ""agree"" to a new system without specifying who manages the space and how the location rotates, we are just legitimizing an unfair distribution of labor.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I think we should avoid the bin house idea completely! It's just a stinky box. Maybe the supervised mornings are better because people actually see what's happening, and it's not that many days a year!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I agree that we should avoid anything that smells, but I'm still very concerned about the cost. If we go for a high-end shelter, the bill might be too heavy for some households to bear.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's be realistic. We have a neighbor who treats the complaint log like a diary and a ward office that loves paperwork. A high-cost, high-maintenance project is just a recipe for more resentment. We need something low-friction.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,May,,"I'm with Shunichi on the low-friction part! If we build some fancy monument to trash, we'll just end up fighting over who has to sweep it. Let's not create a new job for ourselves!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"Low-friction is only a benefit if the friction is shared. If we choose a ""simple"" solution that doesn't address the location, we are simply ignoring the fact that one person's frontage is permanently occupied. We must ensure the burden is rotated.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
61,3,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
