63,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
64,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
65,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I'm voting against Option C! I already told you, the bin house is a stinky trap! We can't just build a box and hope the smell goes away—it'll just get worse in August!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I agree with Rin about the smell, but my biggest worry is the cost. Option C would be a huge financial burden for some of us, and I don't think it's fair.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option C is a bureaucratic suicide mission. Four months of paperwork and five signatures just to build a fancy box for trash? No thank you. Let's pick something that doesn't require a legal team.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,May,,"I'm with the group on C—absolutely not! Between the sweeping fights and the paperwork, it sounds like a nightmare. But @Asuka, if we go with A, who actually manages the schedule? I'm not volunteering to be the one everyone calls!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@May, that is the problem with Option A. It keeps the point in one place, which means one household continues to bear the physical burden while others just ""supervise."" It is not a truly equal arrangement.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, you're right! If it stays in one spot, that person is always the one living next to the trash. But Option B sounds like a big adventure! We get to move the trash point around like a game!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, it does sound more dynamic, but I wonder if moving the point frequently will cause more confusion or complaints. Still, it's much more affordable than Option C, which is a relief.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, confusion is a small price to pay compared to a permanent grudge. Option B is the only one that actually addresses the ""dedicated critic"" problem by sharing the burden. It's rational and, more importantly, keeps us from killing each other.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, you're speaking my language! Rotating the location means no one person becomes the permanent target for the neighborhood critic. Plus, it's way less work than managing a schedule or building a shed. I'm leaning towards B!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"Option B is the only logical choice. It ensures that the physical burden of the refuse point is distributed equally among all five households, rather than remaining a permanent fixture at one person's gate.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Rin,,"I'm totally for Option B! It's fair, it's not a stinky box, and it means no one has to be the ""trash house"" forever. Let's make it a rotation game!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Midori,,I'm leaning towards Option B as well. It avoids the high costs of a structure and seems much fairer to everyone's budget and living space. I think it's the best way to keep the peace.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,It's rare to see this much agreement so quickly. Option B is the only choice that doesn't involve a mountain of paperwork or a financial crisis. Let's just rotate the bins and keep the peace.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,May,,I'm completely sold on B! It's the only option that doesn't turn one of us into a full-time trash manager or a target for complaints. Let's keep it simple and keep rotating!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"I agree. Option B is the only solution that addresses the systemic inequality of the current arrangement. It transforms a permanent burden into a shared responsibility, which is the only way to achieve true fairness.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Rin,,I'm voting for Option B! It's the most fun and the fairest way to do it. No stinky boxes and no one gets stuck with the trash forever! B it is!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Midori,,I'll vote for Option B too. It's the most considerate choice for everyone's wallet and ensures that no one person has to carry the burden alone. I'm glad we found a harmonious solution!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'll vote for Option B. It's the most rational way to neutralize the drama and ensure we can still look each other in the eye. Let's just get this over with.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,May,,I'm voting for Option B! It's the only way to make sure none of us ends up as the neighborhood's unpaid concierge. Let's keep it moving and keep it fair!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I vote for Option B. It is the only arrangement that ensures the physical burden is shared equitably and prevents any single household from being permanently disadvantaged.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
